From 84fee26c08f7560fbebdffa6317f890807a43207 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:32:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Welsh votes/plenary: enumerate full history via
 XMLExport/SeeMore pagination

_fetch_meeting_ids_wales previously used the plain XMLExport filter form,
which always caps out at the current Plenary committee ID's most-recent
~15 rows regardless of any Start/End date sent -- each Senedd term gets a
new committee ID, so that path can never see more than the current term's
meetings, and returns nothing at all when the Senedd is in recess (as
confirmed live 2026-09-05: current term tops out at 15 July, recess runs
20 Jul-13 Sep).

Confirmed live that the site's own "See More" button hits a real,
stateless, cookie-free pagination endpoint --
record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/SeeMore?Committee=0&Page=N -- that walks the
full ~2,900-meeting archive across every committee and term (verified
reaching "Plenary - Sixth Senedd" entries from Feb 2024 by page 50).
Filtering by committee *name* containing "Plenary" instead of by ID is
what reaches multiple terms' history, since the name stays constant while
the ID changes every term.

Rewrote _fetch_meeting_ids_wales to page through that endpoint, reusing
the existing _parse_meeting_rows row-parser per page, stopping once a
page's oldest row (across all committees, since the listing is globally
date-sorted) predates from_date, the site reports no more pages, or a
200-page safety cap is hit. fetch_plenary_business and
fetch_votes_on_division are unchanged -- they already call this method
and inherit the fix automatically.

Verified with a mocked multi-page harness (not live network, which this
container can't reach) covering: pagination stopping at the right page,
cross-page dedup, the "Plenary - Sixth Senedd" naming variant, non-Plenary
row exclusion, votes_only filtering, and newest-first ordering.

Also updated test_scrape.py's Welsh-votes fallback note, which previously
claimed this was structurally impossible via JS-rendered pages -- that's
no longer accurate now that meeting discovery has real historical reach.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Js3FFgf8rFmZ97TBQ51a8w
